STEP BY STEP (the narrative)\
1. Gates open, crowd floods the Domain. Venue mechanics already established \'97 cite, don\'92t re-explain: shelf-company classical-concert permit, Domain Trust wave-through, free ticket in every vinyl dust jacket + Triple Pay reach into Airborne youth, ~half a million on the lawn plus a live stream to every Elvi and the uncloned (established-facts.md). Crowd composition for this scene, per the corrected brief: roughly even Cloudborne/Airborne youth, Elvi a minority among them (limited clone numbers). Do NOT stage any ideological unity or conversion here \'97 explicitly retracted by the author; the crowd is here for the music.\
2. Merch tents swamped: glittering T-shirts, capes, ponchos, Elvi-inspired wigs, stick-on sideburns, and collectible Rock Against Revival \'93Air Guitars.\'94 The joke has a specific mechanism, author\'92s own, verbatim \'97 reproduce exactly: each comes in a branded soft case containing nothing but air, enough to approximate the volume of an electric guitar, and the case\'92s UNLOCK button releases that air through a series of pipes collectively tuned to a drop D power chord. The price gag (a lot of money / nearly nothing) is the punchline; the pipes-and-chord mechanism is what makes it pay off physically rather than just verbally \'97 someone in the scene should actually press the button and let a case go off. Do NOT reintroduce \'93orange glow-orbs\'94 or a \'93velvet case / artisanal air / certified nothing\'94 framing \'97 both are unconfirmed elaboration from an earlier, unaccepted assistant pass; this drop-D mechanism is the author\'92s own confirmed version and supersedes them.\
3. Bar tents: elaborate Elvi-inspired cocktails. Author\'92s specific correction, load-bearing: the problem for the Airborne crowd is SWEETNESS AND FATTINESS, not alcohol content \'97 these drinks carry very little alcohol. Result: puke around the fringes of the crowd as the afternoon heat rises. Keep the mechanism precise \'97 a sugar/heat gag, not a drunk-teenagers gag.\
4. Bands escalate across the day: three-pieces at the start, growing larger set by set. Use this as the scene\'92s internal clock, carrying the reader from gates-open toward the cocktail-hour handoff that opens Scene 2.\
5. Lyric wars: some earlier (lower-billed) bands sing lyrics not written by the Great Teacher. The brief doesn\'92t spell out why for this scene, but the causal engine is already in canon and worth carrying as texture, not exposition: Chanta\'92s ongoing writer\'92s block (chanta.md) means there isn\'92t enough Great-Teacher material to fill a full day\'92s bill, so early acts go outlaw. This is the direct antecedent of the High Elvis\'92s Scene 4 line to Chanta \'97 \'93there would have been less fighting if there were more lyrics\'94 \'97 Scene 1 is the fighting he means. Let this land through a grumbled line or a glance, not a lecture.\
6. Punch-ups: other Elvi run on stage and assault the offending performers; parallel fights break out in the green room. This is the festival\'92s own backstage green room \'97 the same space Scene 4 places Chanta in (\'93carousing with bands and Elvisettes\'85 most of the day\'94) and where his confrontation with the High Elvis over lyrics happens. Keep it as one consistent recurring location across the sequence \'97 and distinct from Truth Central\'92s green room (the PAPER installation used for \'93Chanta Confesses,\'94 established-facts.md), which is a different building entirely.\
7. Crowd reaction: they love the music AND the punch-ups \'97 entertained, not alienated. The Airborne especially mount their own mock, good-natured punch-up. Author\'92s explicit framing: this is crowd mimicry as fun, not ideological conversion \'97 do not write it as evidence the Airborne are being \'93won over\'94 to anything.\
8. The High Elvis intervenes. Register is load-bearing: composed, patient, counselling (the-high-elvis.md) \'97 explicitly NOT the ceremonial song-title bombast voice heard at the Inauguration, which canon flags as inauguration-only. The comic engine of the beat is the mismatch: flat, patient, almost bureaucratic delivery landing in the middle of an actual riot.\
9. He lays down the three laws \'97 reproduce verbatim, do not paraphrase or \'93fix\'94 the repetition in laws 1 and 3 (the tautological loop back to the same law is the joke, not an editing error):\
   \'931) Sing the words of the Great Teacher\
   2) Do not punch up on anyone who does not sing the words of the Great Teacher\
   3) Sing the words of the Great Teacher\'94\
10. Scene ends on the three laws. No aftermath/resolution beat is specified in the brief \'97 don\'92t invent one (e.g. don\'92t show instant crowd obedience or the fighting instantly stopping); leave the effect open or handle it lightly enough not to pre-empt later scenes.\
